From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:14:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] vl: build the memory map once for device creation

Creating a q35 machine with a handful of virtio-pci devices changes the
memory map hundreds of times before the guest runs: 438 flat view
rebuilds were traced on one start, 283 of them while the command line's
devices are added and the machine-done notifiers run.  Outside a
transaction each change regenerates the flat view of every address
space, and a change to guest RAM updates KVM's memory slots.

Wrap device creation and the machine-done notifiers in one memory
transaction.  Board initialization stays outside it: wrapping it too
left KVM's memory slots for the system address space unset and the
guest running without a single exit.  The first system reset, which
copies ROM contents into guest memory, runs from the main loop after
the commit.

A device that read guest memory through an address space while being
realized would see the map from before the transaction.  None of the
devices this machine creates does.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 system/vl.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/system/vl.c b/system/vl.c
index 061cbdf86..9159e9fd6 100644
--- a/system/vl.c
+++ b/system/vl.c
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 #include "qemu/uuid.h"
 #include "system/reset.h"
 #include "system/runstate.h"
+#include "system/memory.h"
 #include "system/runstate-action.h"
 #include "system/seccomp.h"
 #include "system/tcg.h"
@@ -2813,14 +2814,27 @@ static bool qemu_machine_creation_done(Error **errp)
 
 void qmp_x_exit_preconfig(Error **errp)
 {
+    bool ok;
+
     if (phase_check(PHASE_MACHINE_INITIALIZED)) {
         error_setg(errp, "The command is permitted only before machine initialization");
         return;
     }
 
     qemu_init_board();
+    /*
+     * Each device added and each machine-done notifier changes the memory
+     * map, and each change outside a transaction rebuilds the flat view of
+     * every address space.  Build it once, when the machine is complete.  The
+     * board is left out: it sets up the address spaces and the accelerator's
+     * listeners that the commit has to find in place.  The first reset, which
+     * writes the ROMs into guest memory, runs after the commit.
+     */
+    memory_region_transaction_begin();
     qemu_create_cli_devices();
-    if (!qemu_machine_creation_done(errp)) {
+    ok = qemu_machine_creation_done(errp);
+    memory_region_transaction_commit();
+    if (!ok) {
         return;
     }
 
